From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:37:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: link the external
 display domains' bus bridges

A deep sleep powers the J604's external display domains off and on
again: their coprocessor stops, then the CPU, front-end and system
domains go off, and after the sleep they come back before the firmware
restarts from its reset vector. The J604 marked those domains
consumer-switched but left out what the J713 gives them: the bus bridge
link of each system domain and the power-gate retention words of each
CPU domain. The bridge is then never linked again after power-on, and
the restarted coprocessor cannot reach its mailbox: after an aborted
deep sleep both external DCPs failed with "RTKit: endpoint discovery
failed: -62" and stayed dead until a reboot.

Give the system domains their bridge links (the link words 0x800104 into
the external DCP's disp-3 block) and the CPU domains their retention
words, as on the J713. The J604's ADT has the same dcpext0/1 and
dispext0/1 nodes (same reg) and the same pmgr node as the J713's, and
its internal display CPU domain already uses the J713's retention words.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index 75bfda1ffe..497d1a4232 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -395,6 +395,8 @@ &ps_dispext0_sys {
 	status = "okay";
 	apple,firmware-owned;
 	apple,consumer-switched;
+	/* Its bus bridge is unlinked before power-off and linked after power-on. */
+	apple,bridge-link = <&dcpext0 4 0x800104>;
 };
 
 &ps_dispext0_fe {
@@ -406,6 +408,8 @@ &ps_dispext0_fe {
 &ps_dispext0_cpu {
 	apple,firmware-owned;
 	apple,consumer-switched;
+	/* Power-gate retention workaround, as macOS sets it while off. */
+	apple,retention-workaround = <0x256cc 0x03 0x03>, <0x256f0 0x03 0x00>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
@@ -702,6 +706,7 @@ &ps_dispext1_sys {
 	status = "okay";
 	apple,firmware-owned;
 	apple,consumer-switched;
+	apple,bridge-link = <&dcpext1 4 0x800104>;
 };
 
 &ps_dispext1_fe {
@@ -713,6 +718,7 @@ &ps_dispext1_fe {
 &ps_dispext1_cpu {
 	apple,firmware-owned;
 	apple,consumer-switched;
+	apple,retention-workaround = <0x25b4c 0x03 0x03>, <0x25b70 0x03 0x00>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
